 "notes": "p.147 is the right-hand page of a spread whose left page (p.146: Gwalior State + Gird, first half of the list) is not among the scanned leaves 151-158. This page prints no row labels; rows are aligned by counting from the top (37 rows, including all-nil rows) against the facing p.148 (leaf 152). p.147 is typeset without the group spacing that p.148 has, so rows were placed by count, not by y. The placement is confirmed by the Narwar and Sheopur arithmetic (Bhil 58, Rajasthani 307 = 106 + 201, Western Hindi, (2) = 1,009, Eastern Hindi, Gujrati). Row 0 is printed 'Gwalior State' on the facing page and means the grand total for the district column; it is recorded as language 'Total'. The scan is badly degraded: the print is broken into dots, the Bhind and Tonwarghar blocks worst of all, and most of their figures are illegible. Tentative readings are given in 'unreadable' and are not verified. Print inconsistency: for Narwar, row 28 ((2) not proper, 1,009/614/395) exceeds row 29 (Indo-European, 1,007/612/395) by 2 males, but p.151 prints Dravidian nil for Narwar. For Sheopur, row 28 = row 29 (2,630), but p.151 prints Dravidian 2/2 for Sheopur. It looks as if the 2 Dravidian males were set in the wrong column on p.151. CROSS-REFERENCE (Part II, leaf 159, figures legible there; for checking only, NOT copied into '?' cells): mother-tongue totals Bhind: Rajasthani 1,671/1,019/652, Western Hindi 411,575/224,746/186,829, Gujrati 9/6/3; Tonwarghar: Rajasthani 823/469/354, W.Hindi 367,315/203,816/163,499, Gujrati 16/14/2; Sheopur: Rajasthani 53,625/27,706/25,919, W.Hindi 82,285/44,591/37,694, Gujrati 359/211/148; Narwar: Bhil Dialects 58/27/31, Rajasthani 823/513/310, W.Hindi 400,213/210,745/189,468, Gujrati 2/1/1. Part II 'Rajasthani'/'Western Hindi' = ROWS1 group + ROWS2 group (verified exactly for Isagarh and Bhilsa); Part II Gujrati = ROWS1 row 33, Bhil Dialects = row 4."
